## Why This Is Asked

Probes automated containment and rollback for cross-region, multi-tenant Azure SaaS. Emphasizes real-time orchestration across Key Vault, AAD, RBAC, canaries, and traffic routing.

## Key Concepts

- Defender for Cloud UEBA integrations
- Event Grid and Logic Apps for automation
- Per-tenant Key Vault key rotation and token revocation
- Tenant isolation via RBAC and traffic redirection
- Canary controls and sandbox forensics

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo handler for UEBA alert
async function handleUEBAAlert(event) {
  const id = event.tenantId;
  await rotateTenantKeys(id);
  await revokeTenantTokens(id);
  await setTenantRBAC(id, 'read-only');
  await pauseCanariesForTenant(id);
  await redirectTraffic(id, 'lastKnownGood');
  await cloneTenantSandbox(id);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test this workflow end-to-end?
- How would you audit changes made during containment?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests incident-response planning across Defender for Cloud, Azure AD, Key Vault, and cross-subscription governance.

## Key Concepts
- Automated incident response playbooks
- Key Vault secret rotation
- Managed identities and service principals
- Canary rollouts and rollback strategies
- Cross-subscription isolation and monitoring

## Code Example
```javascript
// Rotate secret using Node.js Azure SDK
const { DefaultAzureCredential } = require('@azure/identity');
const { SecretClient } = require('@azure/keyvault-secrets');
const vault = new SecretClient(`https://${'ProdKV'}.vault.azure.net`, new DefaultAzureCredential());
async function rotate(){ const newVal = require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64');
  await vault.setSecret('dbPassword', newVal);
}
rotate().catch(console.error);
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question validates the ability to design an automated security response system for multi-tenant Azure SaaS environments, integrating threat detection with immediate containment and recovery capabilities.

## Key Concepts
- Anomaly detection using Defender for Cloud analytics and Sentinel ML models
- Event Grid-based alert routing and per-tenant processing
- Automated resource isolation via NSG rules, private endpoint restrictions, and conditional access policies
- Key Vault credential rotation and token revocation workflows
- Deployment slot rollback with feature flag coordination
- Comprehensive audit trails across all security actions

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-logic for automated breach response
async function handleSecurityAlert(alert) {
  if (alert.severity > 3) {
    await isolateTenantResources(alert.tenantId);
    await rotateCompromisedCredentials(alert.tenantId);
    await initiateSafeRollback(alert.tenantId);
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design cross-service, tenant-aware, tamper-resistant logging with strict retention and quick rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Tamper-evident logging; per-tenant key management; HMAC; Key Vault rotation
- Multi-service sinks; Log Analytics and ADLS Gen2 immutable storage
- Real-time integrity checks; Event Hubs; Canary rollout; incident response

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: sign and write log
function signAndWrite(log, tenantId){
  const key = getKeyFromKV(tenantId);
  const signature = hmacSHA256(log, key);
  writeToSink({log, signature, tenantId});
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify integrity without exposing keys?
- How would you handle key compromise and replay attacks?
